  "description": "Fast in-process video and audio for .NET through FFmpeg's libraries: frames at a size and pixel format, the bytes ffmpeg's scale+format filters give, with exact seeking, thumbnails, fps and parallel reads; audio samples, filter graphs, spectral statistics, waveform peaks; writing MP3/AAC/WAV and (with x264) H.264, byte for byte ffmpeg's output; stream copy; probing. No ffmpeg process, no pipes, no allocation per frame. Needs FFmpeg 8's shared libraries: the FrameReader.Native.<rid> packages (H.264 needs a build with libx264 of your own).",
